  }
  .stat-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .stat-label { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .stat-value { font-weight: 600; color: #fff; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stat-pct { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 12px; margin-left: 0.5rem; }

  /* ── REGIME BAR ── */
  .regime-bar-container {
    margin: 1rem 0;
    display: flex;
    height: 48px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .regime-segment {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fff;
    flex-direction: column;
    transition: flex-basis 0.3s;
    min-width: 40px;
  }
  .regime-segment .seg-label { font-size: 9px; font-weight: 400; opacity: 0.8; margin-top: 1px; }
  .regime-leo { background: #388bfd; }
  .regime-meo { background: #3fb950; }
  .regime-geo { background: #f0883e; }
  .regime-heo { background: #bc8cff; }

  /* ── CALLOUT ── */
  .callout {
    background: var(--surface2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .callout strong { color: var(--accent); }

  /* ── TWO COLUMN ── */
  .two-col { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; }

  /* ── FOOTER ── */
  footer {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
    padding: 0 2rem;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  /* ── BADGE ── */
  .badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .badge-starlink { background: rgba(163,113,247,0.2); color: var(--starlink); border: 1px solid rgba(163,113,247,0.4); }
  .badge-oneweb { background: rgba(63,185,80,0.15); color: var(--accent2); border: 1px solid rgba(63,185,80,0.3); }
  .badge-geo { background: rgba(240,136,62,0.15); color: var(--accent3); border: 1px solid rgba(240,136,62,0.3); }

  /* ── CONCLUSION LIST ── */
  .takeaway-list { list-style: none; }
  .takeaway-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .takeaway-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .takeaway-num {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    line-height: 1;
    min-width: 32px;
  }
  .takeaway-text strong { color: #fff; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  .takeaway-text { color: var(--text-muted); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .kpi-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .chart-grid, .chart-grid-3, .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="eyebrow">CelesTrak / NORAD TLE Catalog · April 2026</div>
  <h1>Active Satellites in Earth Orbit</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">2026 Catalog Analysis · 14,875 active spacecraft · Space Industry & Policy Reference</div>
</header>

<main>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     KPI STRIP
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="kpi-strip">
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="kpi-value">14,875</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Total Active Satellites</div>
    <div class="kpi-sub kpi-accent">CelesTrak / NORAD TLE</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="kpi-value">86.5%</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">LEO Share</div>
    <div class="kpi-sub">12,860 of 14,875</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="kpi-value">10,083</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Starlink Constellation</div>
    <div class="kpi-sub kpi-accent">67.8% of all active</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="kpi-value">53.2°</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Median Inclination</div>
    <div class="kpi-sub">All orbital regimes</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="kpi-value">13,461</div>
    <div class="kpi-label">Launched Since 2020</div>
    <div class="kpi-sub kpi-accent">90.5% of active fleet</div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 1 — CATALOG OVERVIEW
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">01</span>
    <h2>Catalog Overview &amp; Key Figures</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      The CelesTrak / NORAD Two-Line Element (TLE) catalog captures <strong style="color:#fff">14,875 active satellites</strong>
      as of March–April 2026. The data reflects orbital elements updated continuously by the U.S. Space Force's
      18th Space Defense Squadron, with epoch dates concentrated in March 2026 — confirming data freshness.
      The catalog excludes debris and non-operational objects.
    </p>
    <div class="chart-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Mean Motion Distribution (orbits/day)</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="chart-mm"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Inclination Distribution (°)</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="chart-inc"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <div class="chart-title">Eccentricity Distribution</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="chart-ecc"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 2 — ORBITAL REGIME CLASSIFICATION
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">02</span>
    <h2>Orbital Regime Classification</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      Orbit regime is assigned using <strong style="color:#fff">MEAN_MOTION thresholds</strong> (orbits/revolution/day):
      LEO above 14.0, GEO between 0.9–1.1, MEO in between, and HEO below 0.9.
    </p>
    <div class="regime-bar-container">
      <div class="regime-segment regime-leo" style="flex-basis: 86.5%;">
        <span>86.5%</span><span class="seg-label">LEO</span>
      </div>
      <div class="regime-segment regime-meo" style="flex-basis: 9.5%;">
        <span>9.5%</span><span class="seg-label">MEO</span>
      </div>
      <div class="regime-segment regime-geo" style="flex-basis: 4.0%;">
        <span>4.0%</span><span class="seg-label">GEO</span>
      </div>
      <div class="regime-segment regime-heo" style="flex-basis: 0.1%;">
        <span>0.1%</span><span class="seg-label">HEO</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="two-col" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Regime Count Comparison</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="chart-regime-pie"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Regime Composition</div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">LEO  ·  Mean Motion &gt; 14.0 rev/day</span><span class="stat-value">12,860 <span class="stat-pct">(86.5%)</span></span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">MEO  ·  1.1 &lt; Mean Motion ≤ 14.0</span><span class="stat-value">1,408 <span class="stat-pct">(9.5%)</span></span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">GEO  ·  0.9 ≤ Mean Motion ≤ 1.1</span><span class="stat-value">596 <span class="stat-pct">(4.0%)</span></span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">HEO  ·  Mean Motion &lt; 0.9</span><span class="stat-value">11 <span class="stat-pct">(0.1%)</span></span></div>
        <div class="stat-row" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--border); margin-top: 0.5rem; padding-top: 0.75rem;">
          <span class="stat-label"><strong>Total</strong></span>
          <span class="stat-value"><strong>14,875</strong></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>LEO Dominance.</strong> The 86.5% LEO share reflects the extraordinary scale of mega-constellation
      deployment — primarily Starlink, OneWeb, and Planet — which concentrate in shells between ~550 km and ~1,200 km altitude.
      GEO (4.0%) remains a premium, high-value orbit reserved for communications, weather, and intelligence satellites.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 3 — MAJOR CONSTELLATIONS & OPERATORS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">03</span>
    <h2>Major Constellation &amp; Operator Breakdown</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      SpaceX's Starlink constellation dominates the active satellite population, accounting for
      <strong style="color:#fff">67.8% of all active satellites</strong>. The remaining ~32% is split across
      commercial, civil, and government operators. This extreme concentration fundamentally skews orbital
      statistics toward LEO, low-inclination shells.
    </p>
    <div class="chart-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Top 10 Operators by Satellite Count</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="chart-operators"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Starlink Shell Inclination Breakdown (n=10,083)</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="chart-starlink-inc"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <div class="chart-title">Operator Share — Excluding Starlink</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="chart-ops-excl-starlink"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <strong>Starlink Shell Strategy.</strong> Starlink operates multiple orbital shells differentiated by inclination:
      the 53.2° shell (~4,840 sats) covers mid-latitude global coverage; the 40° shell (~3,656 sats) adds polar coverage;
      and the 97.6° shell (~872 sats) provides high-latitude reinforcement. Shells at 70° (~506 sats) and 65° (~209 sats)
      address regional coverage gaps. This multi-shell approach makes Starlink's inclination distribution multimodal,
      pulling the overall LEO median toward ~53°.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 4 — LAUNCH YEAR TRENDS (PRIMARY)
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number" style="color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent);">04</span>
    <h2 style="color: var(--accent);">Launch Year Trends — The Great Acceleration</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      The active satellite population tells a stark story of recent acceleration. Of the 14,875 active satellites,
      <strong style="color:#fff">13,461 (90.5%) were launched since 2020</strong>. The 2025 active fleet alone
      accounts for 4,329 satellites — more than the combined total of all spacecraft launched before 2018.
    </p>

    <div class="chart-full">
      <div class="chart-title">Active Satellites by Launch Year (full history, 1964–2026)</div>
      <div class="chart-wrap" style="height: 320px;">
        <canvas id="chart-launch-full"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Launch Activity — 2015 to 2026 (Recent Era)</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="chart-launch-recent"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Cumulative Active Population</div>
        <div class="chart-wrap">
          <canvas id="chart-cumulative"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <div style="background: var(--surface2); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem; text-align: center;">
        <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #fff;">90.5%</div>
        <div style="font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.25rem;">Share launched 2020–2026</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background: var(--surface2); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem; text-align: center;">
        <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent);">4,329</div>
        <div style="font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.25rem;">Active sats from 2025 alone</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background: var(--surface2); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem; text-align: center;">
        <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent2);">~8.7×</div>
        <div style="font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.25rem;">Growth since 2020 (498 → 4,329)</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background: var(--surface2); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1rem; text-align: center;">
        <div style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--starlink);">10,083</div>
        <div style="font-size: 10px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.25rem;">Starlink sats (all post-2019)</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Policy Implication.</strong> The launch cadence has shifted from a slow-building orbital population
      (roughly 50–100 new active satellites/year throughout the 2000s–2010s) to a regime of thousands per year,
      driven almost entirely by commercial LEO constellations. Regulatory frameworks, spectrum allocation, and
      orbital debris mitigation rules written before 2018 face a fundamentally different operational environment today.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 5 — ORBITAL PARAMETER DEEP DIVE
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">05</span>
    <h2>Orbital Parameter Deep Dive</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">MEAN_MOTION Statistics</div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Minimum</span><span class="stat-value">0.2834 rev/day</span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Maximum</span><span class="stat-value">16.3016 rev/day</span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Mean</span><span class="stat-value">14.33 rev/day</span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Median</span><span class="stat-value">14.87 rev/day</span></div>
        <div class="stat-row" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 0.5rem; padding-top: 0.75rem;">
          <span class="stat-label">LEO median (~550 km)</span><span class="stat-value">~15.1 rev/day</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-row">
          <span class="stat-label">GEO orbital period</span><span class="stat-value">~1,436 min (sidereal day)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="chart-title">Inclination Statistics</div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Minimum</span><span class="stat-value">0.00°</span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Maximum</span><span class="stat-value">149.86°</span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Mean</span><span class="stat-value">54.7°</span></div>
        <div class="stat-row"><span class="stat-label">Median</span><span class="stat-value">53.2°</span></div>
        <div class="stat-row" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 0.5rem; padding-top: 0.75rem;">
          <span class="stat-label">Peak concentration</span><span class="stat-value">50°–60° (5,399 sats)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-row">
          <span class="stat-label">Polar orbits (≥80°)</span><span class="stat-value">1,602 (10.8%)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
      <strong>Inclination Modal Structure.</strong> The inclination distribution is bimodal: the peak at
      <strong style="color:#fff">50°–60° (5,399 sats, 36.3%)</strong> reflects Starlink's dominant 53.2° shell;
      a secondary peak at <strong style="color:#fff">40°–50° (3,915 sats, 26.3%)</strong> blends Starlink's 40°
      shell with OneWeb's ~86° polar constellation and mid-inclination LEO operators.
      The ~0°–10° band (584 sats) is dominated by GEO-belt satellites in equatorial orbits.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 6 — CONCLUSIONS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">06</span>
    <h2>Key Takeaways &amp; Outlook</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="section-body">
    <ul class="takeaway-list">
      <li>
        <div class="takeaway-num">1</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">
          <strong>Mega-constellations have fundamentally restructured Earth orbit.</strong>
          A single operator — SpaceX Starlink — accounts for 67.8% of all active satellites.
          The top five operators (Starlink, OneWeb, Planet, Cosmos, Iridium) represent ~74% of the active population.
          Spectrum allocation and orbital congestion policy cannot be discussed without Starlink as the central case.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="takeaway-num">2</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">
          <strong>LEO is the operational frontier.</strong> With 86.5% of active satellites in LEO,
          medium and high Earth orbit regimes remain relatively uncongested. The crowding challenge
          is almost exclusively a LEO problem — and within LEO, concentrated in two inclination bands
          (40°–60°) at altitudes between ~550 km and ~1,200 km.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="takeaway-num">3</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">
          <strong>The launch growth curve is near-vertical since 2020.</strong> From 498 active satellites
          launched in 2020 to 4,329 in 2025 — an 8.7× increase in five years. This rate of change
          outpaces the revision cycles of ITU spectrum regulations and national licensing frameworks.
          If 2025's pace continues, the active LEO population could exceed 20,000 by 2030.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="takeaway-num">4</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">
          <strong>Debris risk is increasingly a Starlink-specific concern.</strong> With 10,083 active
          Starlink satellites, SpaceX's own conjunction management practices effectively define the
          debris environment in heavily used shells. The FCC's 2022 rule requiring deorbit within
          5 years of mission completion for LEO satellites below 2,000 km is a significant step,
          but enforcement and international harmonization remain open questions.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="takeaway-num">5</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">
          <strong>Inclination stratification creates distinct congestion zones.</strong> Starlink's
          multi-shell strategy (40°, 53°, 65°, 70°, 97° shells) deliberately fills different
          latitudinal coverage bands — but this also means specific inclination corridors face
          disproportionate conjunction density. Operators planning new constellations face a
          de facto zoning problem: certain shells are becoming crowded while others remain available.
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

</main>

