      the 53.2° shell (~4,840 sats) covers mid-latitude global coverage; the 40° shell (~3,656 sats) adds polar coverage;
      and the 97.6° shell (~872 sats) provides high-latitude reinforcement. Shells at 70° (~506 sats) and 65° (~209 sats)
      address regional coverage gaps. This multi-shell approach makes Starlink's inclination distribution multimodal,
      pulling the overall LEO median toward ~53°.
    </div>
  </div>
