<div class="callout">
<strong>Policy Implication.</strong> The launch cadence has shifted from ~50&ndash;100 new active satellites/year throughout the 2000s&ndash;2010s to thousands per year, driven almost entirely by commercial LEO constellations. Regulatory frameworks, spectrum allocation, and orbital debris mitigation rules written before 2018 face a fundamentally different operational environment. If 2025's pace continues, the active LEO population could exceed 20,000 by 2030.
</div>
</div>
</div>

